-- ===== Adversarial probes =====

-- EXPECT: the program ends with a value left on the stack that is never freed
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- box is linear: must be consumed, not abandoned
42 box

-- EXPECT: 'free' takes 'b copyable box
-- EXPECT: dict is not a box.
-- free rejects dicts at type time
dict free

-- ===== protocol constraints =====
-- EXPECT: 'mod' takes int int
-- EXPECT: float is not int.
-- mod is Integral: floats are not
1.0 2.0 mod

-- EXPECT: 'default' takes {'ok 'a copyable 'no 'b copyable} either
-- EXPECT: int is not a list.
-- ...and a string fallback cannot stand in for an int payload either
[1 2 3] pop "str" default len drop

-- ===== runtime panics: programmer errors that types cannot see =====
-- EXPECT: div: division by zero
-- division by zero
1 0 div drop

-- EXPECT: mod: division by zero
-- modulo by zero
1 0 mod drop

-- EXPECT: expected 'ok tagged, got 'no tagged
-- must on a 'no value
none must drop

-- EXPECT: get: index 99 out of bounds (len 3)
-- index out of bounds, unwrapped
[1 2 3] 99 get must drop

-- EXPECT: peek: index 99 out of bounds (len 3)
-- ...but peek must still panics
[1 2 3] 99 peek must drop drop

-- ===== aliasing and linearity =====
-- EXPECT: 'insert' takes 'a copyable dict str 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- a tagged box stays linear, so insert's guard still sees it
dict "k" 42 box 'x tag insert drop

-- EXPECT: 'drop' takes 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- the same laundering, one step earlier: dropping a tagged box leaked it
42 box 'x tag drop

-- EXPECT: 'dup' takes 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- and `dup` on one produced two references to a single BoxData
42 box 'x tag dup drop drop

-- EXPECT: 'push' takes 'a copyable list 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- a list is as stackable as a dict; push has to reject it for the same reason
[] 42 box 'x tag push drop

-- EXPECT: stack overflow
-- a literal pushed onto a full operand stack
0 2097151 range 7 print

-- EXPECT: C stack exhausted printing a deeply nested value
-- print recurses once per nesting level
[] 'n tag 20000 ([] swap push 'n tag) repeat print

-- EXPECT: C stack exhausted while comparing a deeply nested value
-- val_equal recurses once per nesting level
[] 'n tag 30000 ([] swap push 'n tag) repeat dup eq print

